n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed with its last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources, sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report, then completed runs older than the configured age threshold are listed together with their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given the stale pipeline-run report, when an administrator changes the age threshold configuration, then the report reflects the new threshold without code changes.\n- Given either report, when an administrator exports it as CSV, then the CSV contains the same rows and columns as the on-screen report.\n- Both reports are scoped per project and accessible to cluster administrators.\n- The idle-workbench report is verified against live notebook-controller activity data, confirming the Notebooks component needs no code changes for this feature (passive-component validation).\n- The stale pipeline-run report is verified against live Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata, confirming the Data Science Pipelines component needs no code changes for this feature (passive-component validation).\n- No automated reclamation, deletion, or cost/chargeback functionality is introduced (out-of-scope boundary).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) from notebook controller activity tracking — fully covered by this epic's idle-workbench report scope.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata — fully covered by this epic's stale pipeline-run report scope.\n- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)**: CSV export of either report — bundled here rather than split because the export shares the same report UI surfaces and data structures as the P1 reports; it is a presentation mode of the same report surface, and splitting it would require a second pass over the same views and aggregation code.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30094,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93c470ecfc2aaf24","agent_id":"afc41fc47975a73ef","session_id":"e029b94f-474c-45be-acc9-edc4977b567a","uuid":"6c26b491-6783-4475-9df7-8971caa1fcd3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:13:14.727Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016 into epics"}
