{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-965fbb6bca396d7f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers idle resource reporting in the RHOAI web console: a per-project view showing which resources are sitting idle so cluster administrators can reclaim capacity with confidence. It covers two report views — idle workbenches (from the notebook controller's activity tracking) and stale pipeline runs (from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata) — plus CSV export of either report.\n34\t\n35\tThe data sources require no code changes: the notebook controller already tracks last-activity timestamps and Kubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata. This epic surfaces that data in the console; it does not implement automated reclamation or deletion (explicitly out of scope).\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console showing, for each workbench: last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources. Sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n40\t- Stale pipeline-run report in the web console showing completed pipeline runs older than a configurable age threshold, with their retained artifacts. Sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run completion metadata.\n41\t- Administrator-configurable age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report.\n42\t- CSV export of either report, with exported rows matching the on-screen report.\n43\t- Validate during implementation that the notebook controller's activity data and the Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata are consumable by the console in the form these reports need; if an exposure gap is found, surface it back to the owning teams rather than working around it silently.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the idle-workbench report, then each workbench is listed with its last activity timestamp, owner, and reserved resources, sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n48\t- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the stale pipeline-run report, then completed runs older than the configured age threshold are listed together with their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n49\t- Given the stale pipeline-run report, when an administrator changes the age threshold configuration, then the report reflects the new threshold without code changes.\n50\t- Given either report, when an administrator exports it as CSV, then the CSV contains the same rows and columns as the on-screen report.\n51\t- Both reports are scoped per project and accessible to cluster administrators.\n52\t- The idle-workbench report is verified against live notebook-controller activity data, confirming the Notebooks component needs no code changes for this feature (passive-component validation).\n53\t- The stale pipeline-run report is verified against live Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata, confirming the Data Science Pipelines component needs no code changes for this feature (passive-component validation).\n54\t- No automated reclamation, deletion, or cost/chargeback functionality is introduced (out-of-scope boundary).\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) from notebook controller activity tracking — fully covered by this epic's idle-workbench report scope.\n59\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata — fully covered by this epic's stale pipeline-run report scope.\n60\t- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)**: CSV export of either report — bundled here rather than split because the export shares the same report UI surfaces and data structures as the P1 reports; it is a presentation mode of the same report surface, and splitting it would require a second pass over the same views and aggregation code.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fb8b9fb617983ad","agent_id":"a0996fd62631ebff7","session_id":"e029b94f-474c-45be-acc9-edc4977b567a","uuid":"e5ff2f6f-b165-4210-bda8-9c151bef7242","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:14:56.855Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-965fbb6bca396d7f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
