pe boundary (no automated reclamation or deletion, no cost/chargeback).\n43\t- Screenshots and configuration references for the reports, updated to match the implemented feature.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- A published documentation topic explains both reports, the data each presents, the configurable stale-run age threshold, and the CSV export.\n48\t- The topic documents safe, manual reclamation steps for idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs, and does not describe any automated reclamation or deletion capability (out-of-scope boundary).\n49\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented console feature by the owning team, and any inaccuracies found in review are corrected before publication.\n50\t- Screenshots and configuration instructions match the shipped behavior of the reports.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-4 (P2)**: documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps — fully covered by this epic's documentation topic.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fb8b9fb617983ad","agent_id":"a0996fd62631ebff7","session_id":"e029b94f-474c-45be-acc9-edc4977b567a","uuid":"4cac5bd4-7946-4985-9ff0-bdf4aa372cea","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:14:57.443Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7085ac775bf044e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
